What I did: Explicitly enabled prompt caching on all three agent construction paths in src/agent_builder.rs:

1. **`configure_agent()** (used by build_agent() and build_editor_agent()) — added with_cache_config(CacheConfig { enabled: true, strategy: CacheStrategy::Auto })` 
2. `build_side_agent()` — same cache config added to the builder chain
3. `build_architect_agent()` — same cache config added to the builder chain

**The test:** test_cache_config_enabled_on_all_agents verifies all three paths produce agents with cache_config.enabled == true and cache_config.strategy == CacheStrategy::Auto.

Why this matters: yoagent 0.8's CacheStrategy::Auto places cache_control: ephemeral breakpoints on the system prompt, last tool definition, and second-to-last message — exactly what Anthropic needs to cache the conversation prefix. This can reduce input token costs by ~90% for cached content across multi-turn sessions (yoyo's primary use case). The default happened to already be `enabled: true`, but being explicit documents the intent and guards against future library changes.

